@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy Policy";
}

<h1>@ViewData["Title"]</h1>
<p><strong>Last updated:</strong> September 2026</p>

<p>
    DohFlo is a portfolio demonstration created to show software development
    skills to potential employers, recruiters, and other invited reviewers.
    It is not a commercial banking, accounting, or financial service.
</p>

<h2 class="h4 mt-4">Information used by this site</h2>
<p>
    Public pages do not ask visitors to submit personal financial information.
    When sign-in is enabled, the application may process the username or email
    address needed to authenticate an authorized visitor. The web server may
    also create routine technical logs, such as request times, error details,
    browser information, and IP addresses, for security and troubleshooting.
</p>

<h2 class="h4 mt-4">Demonstration data</h2>
<p>
    The accounts, payees, categories, balances, and transactions shown in the
    shared demo account are fictional. Visitors must not enter real bank account
    numbers, payment card information, passwords, Social Security numbers, or
    other sensitive personal information.
</p>

<h2 class="h4 mt-4">How information is used</h2>
<p>
    Information is used only to operate, secure, test, maintain, and improve the
    demonstration application. DohFlo does not sell personal information.
</p>

<h2 class="h4 mt-4">Data retention and security</h2>
<p>
    Technical logs and account information are retained only as needed for the
    operation and security of the project. Reasonable safeguards are used, but
    no internet service can guarantee absolute security.
</p>

<h2 class="h4 mt-4">Policy changes</h2>
<p>
    This policy may be updated when the application adds or changes features,
    hosting providers, analytics, authentication, or other services. The date at
    the top of this page will be revised when material changes are made.
</p>

<h2 class="h4 mt-4">Questions</h2>
<p>
    For questions about this portfolio project, please use the contact method
    through which the DohFlo demonstration link was provided.
</p>

